# Citation metadata for NMAFC.
#
# NOTE: there is deliberately NO `preferred-citation` entry. No paper, preprint,
# or submission for NMAFC exists. Adding one would imply peer-reviewed
# scientific validation that does not exist. This file cites the SOFTWARE only.
#
# If a paper is published, add `preferred-citation` at that time.
#
# The LoCoMo benchmark dataset used in the reported results is a SEPARATE work
# with its own citation and a non-commercial licence. See NOTICE and the entry
# below — do not conflate the two.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NMAFC in academic work, please cite the software and the version you used."
title: "NMAFC: Neuromorphic Memory Architecture for Conversational AI"
abstract: >-
  A two-tier, biologically-inspired memory substrate for LLM agents. Conversation
  turns are compacted at write time into atomic assertions with resolved absolute
  temporal anchors and entity links; working memory decays exponentially per
  conversational turn and consolidates through long-term potentiation into a
  searchable cold archive. Retrieval fuses dense, lexical, and graph-expansion
  channels by reciprocal rank fusion and hydrates a dual-layer context of
  compacted facts plus verbatim source turns. Distributed under
  PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0 (non-commercial use only).
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-02"
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0

authors:
  - family-names: Edogun
    given-names: Osamudiamen
    email: edogunosamudiamen@gmail.com
    orcid: ""
  - family-names: Obigwe
    given-names: Joshua
    email: josicoded@gmail.com
    orcid: ""

repository-code: "https://github.com/blok-hamster/nmafc"
url: "https://github.com/blok-hamster/nmafc"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - agent memory
  - long-term memory
  - temporal reasoning
  - retrieval
  - knowledge graph
  - context management

